lines+=['','All games have600s horizons and bridge legality. Each column covers eight layouts,two action RNGs each. Validation layouts never enter training,but are used for selection;these are not independent final-confirmation results. Paired intervals resample cities. No reliable reference improvement established.','', 'The whole-city version outperformed gated control on the repeated set (+27.625,95%[4.6875,52.6875]),but gains versus reference are uncertain,and separate-city scoring count falls15→14. Finite-cutoff final repeated delta−4.75,95%[−21.3125,7.625];separate delta−9.5,[−41.5625,28.125]. The cutoff hypothesis did not produce a score fix.','', '## What watching revealed','', 'The failed reference anchor spends all initial roads by26s on branches/loops before completing service,then ends with0 at151.15s. Whole-city final reaches175 at600s with first delivery32s. The second anchor changes158→172. However32 fresh action RNGs on the first opening give27/32 success for both reference and final. One favorable replay is not a reliable repair. Finite-horizon anchor scores20 and168.','', 'At16 inspected initial states,the whole-city actor changes mean Wait probability by−0.016868,while conditional-road TV averages0.000370. The first differing action on the improved replay can be reproduced by changing only Wait mass in the joint categorical sampler. This supports investigating weak road-choice adaptation;it does not prove a sole global cause or establish that a longer run cannot learn.','', '## Changes and checks','', 'Optional whole-city correction removes the established-service gate without changing initial weights/actions/values. Repeated-city training is optional;defaults remain unchanged. Optional finite horizon changes learning termination semantics only for that diagnostic. Native rewards remain deliveries;no planner,teacher actions,new reward term or physics change.','', 'Checks:256 exact initial actor/value states;opening gradient0 gated versus2.86916 whole;reset cycle/bypass;three policy/reporting tests;first8 pre-update episodes exactly matched;729-transition finite-horizon parity;post-training allowed-weight/finite/optimizer audits. All three runs completed1024/1024 updates. Figures were visually inspected. Replay selector/timeline logic passed six combinations in a JavaScript VM with stub DOM/canvas,not a browser rendering test. Sampled snapshots are labeled frames,not policy decisions.','', '## Artifacts and remaining question','', '[Interactive comparison of both preselected games and all three policies](compare-play.html). [Measured source results](results.json). [Plan and chronological choices](PLAN.md). [Full experiment history](../../../training/EXPERIMENT_HISTORY.md). Weights/native binaries are local-only;see local-artifacts.json and manifest.json.','', 'Current strongest remaining lead: road-choice adaptation is weak at the inspected opening states,while Wait changes can create visually dramatic but unreliable trajectory changes. Next work should measure/target road-choice learning and exploration on repeatable native decisions,then test untouched layouts. These small one-training-seed trials do not establish impossibility or justify promising overnight score gains.']
